Distinguish conversion, yield, selectivity, recovery, and purity (@gc-yield: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @general-chemistry, #source "../sources/Chemistry-OpenStax.lingua#r_02Y5N2VMTTPBDSNYPD4Z26EZ94", #source "../sources/Chem1-Lower.lingua#r_0NFQA43WZVMECZY6SKZJMRXWBZ", #general-chemistry "../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/practice/Concentrations-and-bases.lingua#r_0XCSBEG82Y6TYKX1Z28R693AY5", #industrial-chemistry "../../industrial-chemistry/balances/Conversion-selectivity-isolated-yield-and-usable-output.lingua#r_59JNS3Q481HSMKY7ZHFFVJFVG6") { r_73PW18H0EQATWC20EC95V9D9M3
**Read:** [Chemistry 2e — Flowers, Theopold, Langley, and Robinson](../sources/Chemistry-OpenStax.lingua#r_02Y5N2VMTTPBDSNYPD4Z26EZ94), chapter 4’s reaction-yield treatment and exercises; [Chem1 General Chemistry Virtual Textbook — Stephen Lower](../sources/Chem1-Lower.lingua#r_0NFQA43WZVMECZY6SKZJMRXWBZ), stoichiometry and material-accounting examples.

A measured product amount can answer several different questions. Conversion describes consumption of a specified reactant relative to its chosen initial or inlet amount. Yield compares a desired product with a clearly defined reference amount. Selectivity compares competing products or pathways under a stated basis. Recovery tracks how much of a specified component reaches a selected output. Purity characterizes that output's composition.

Define the denominator for every percentage. A product can be very pure while containing only a small fraction of the incoming target component. A reactant can convert extensively into unwanted products. Loss during isolation differs from failure to form the product. Without separate information, a low collected yield does not identify which mechanism dominated.

Use species and element balances to keep these quantities consistent. Include unreacted feed, secondary products, solvent/water, dust or gas, accumulated material, and measured/unmeasured streams where relevant. A mass balance that appears to exceed 100% may reveal a basis error, contamination, retained solvent, a wrong species identity, or uncertainty rather than extraordinary reaction performance.

**Work:** design an original small hypothetical balance with a desired product, an alternative reaction product, unreacted material, and an isolation loss. Define and calculate conversion, a chosen product yield, selectivity, component recovery, and product purity. Reconstruct the result independently and explain which measurements would separate formation from collection loss in a real study.

Read the relevant whole textbook chapter and revisit the generic quantitative balance examples. Later specialist processes will require their own chemical mechanisms and separation models; this Record provides shared language for comparing their outcomes without confusing a favorable percentage with an entire process account.

**Continue:** [Concentrations, moisture, and changing the basis](../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/practice/Concentrations-and-bases.lingua#r_0XCSBEG82Y6TYKX1Z28R693AY5).

